# Context:
This page discusses how AEO can transform organizations and how to prepare for those changes.

# Text:
How AEO transforms organizations
AEO has the potential to transform the way
organizations are structured and how they operate.
By breaking down silos and fostering collaboration,
AEO can unlock new levels of efficiency, creativity,
and customer-centricity.
To fully realize the benefits of AEO,
organizations must be willing to embrace change
and adapt their cultures, processes, and
technologies. This requires a shift in mindset
from channel-centric to customer-centric, as well
as a willingness to experiment and learn.
Preparing your organization for AEO
1. Assess your current state:
Identify the gaps between your current
organization structure and the AEO model.
2. Define your vision for AEO:
Establish clear goals and objectives for your AEO
implementation.
3. Develop a roadmap:
Create a detailed plan for how you will transition
to AEO, including timelines, milestones, and
resource allocation.
4. Invest in training and development:
Provide your employees with the skills and
knowledge they need to succeed in an AEO
environment.
5. Foster a culture of collaboration:
Encourage communication and teamwork across
departments and teams.
6. Embrace experimentation:
Be willing to try new approaches and learn from
your mistakes.
7. Monitor and measure your progress:
Track your key performance indicators (KPIs) and
make adjustments as needed.
