**Context:** This page continues the discussion of four key moves to drive AEO success, focusing on long-term execution. It emphasizes the importance of establishing clear goals and metrics aligned with business outcomes.

**Text:**
**Move toward long-term execution**

The principles and approaches we’ve outlined here won’t matter if your AEO ambitions are short-sighted.
Because an effective AEO program requires constant attention to optimization, consider these questions:

**1. How will you set goals and metrics around real business outcomes?**

The right business metrics should be tied to AEO’s impact on revenue, cost savings, and brand reputation.
For example, if your team’s task is to drive customer care automation, you can establish goals related to
customer care capacity.

**2. How will you measure the impact of AEO against current marketing efforts?**

If you're generating sales with an AEO program, you must decide how to measure it against the performance
of paid campaigns. An incremental lift analysis can determine whether new customers are being acquired
through AEO.

**3. How will you evolve your AEO strategy as Al platforms and algorithms change?**

AEO is a moving target. To keep up with changes in Al, your team needs to be committed to learning the
latest best practices and applying them to your strategy.

**4. How will you incorporate AEO into your broader marketing tech stack?**

AEO should be integrated into your broader marketing strategy. For example, you can use AEO to generate
leads for your sales team or to drive traffic to your website.

AEO: The time is now
