- Context: This page discusses the AEO Divide, focusing on the evolution of organic search and the skills marketers need to meet the demands of AEO.
- Text: The AEO Divide
Organic search is evolving beyond SERP
rankings.
Marketers must meet the demands of
Answer Engine Optimization (AEO)
to keep pace with a changing search landscape.
But are marketers equipped with the
right skillset?
As search engines evolve from information
retrieval to comprehensive answer engines,
traditional keyword-centric SEO alone is no
longer enough to maintain organic search
visibility. Marketers must embrace
Answer Engine Optimization (AEO).
This modern approach to search marketing
focuses on providing high-quality, comprehensive,
and valuable answers across a wider range of
surfaces, not just optimizing for a single
ranking position on the Search Engine
Results Page (SERP). This requires a shift in
focus and a broader set of skills for marketers.
36%
of marketers say they have the skills to
adapt to a modern search landscape.
64%
do not feel prepared to meet the
demands of Answer Engine Optimization.
Key AEO skill gaps
Content management
Reporting & analytics
Technical SEO
Structured data
